          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"2aa74102d9e3011cd0032533\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required user request covering two exchanges; the stated boot fallback applies because an exchange to identical options is not permitted by the exchange rule.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0081\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0005\"}],\"rationale\":\"Interpret the conditional boot request, clarify the subjective puzzle theme if needed, and authenticate by name and ZIP because the user does not remember their email.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":2,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional boot exchange: the documented fallback matches an available, different-option variant.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0081\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0088\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0313\"}],\"rationale\":\"Find the boot order and eligible leather, waterproof size-9 variant, check delivered status and payment method, obtain confirmation, then bind the IDs to the exchange.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":2}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_002\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required puzzle exchange in the second order; the reference identifies the intended fantasy variant.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0091\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0279\"}],\"rationale\":\"Identify the original puzzle's piece count and difficulty, verify the available 1,000-piece intermediate variant and the user's theme preference, then confirm and submit the exchange.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The sufficient path includes authentication, discovery across two orders and product catalogs, clarification and confirmation, and two separate exchanges. Once the same-spec boot request is ruled out, it does not add an attempted write or a further repair path.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0087\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0081\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must reconcile the same-spec request with the different-option rule, apply the conditional boot preference, and preserve the puzzle's difficulty while reducing its pieces and interpreting its theme.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0081\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0261\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Authentication and user, order, and product lookups feed distinct order/item/variant/payment bindings into two exchange calls; each write uses paired item-ID lists.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0102\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0194\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0183\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0188\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0160\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0084\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Authentication precedes order discovery; each delivered-order check, variant selection, payment-method choice, and explicit confirmation precedes its write. The two orders require separate, linked exchange submissions, not one combined call.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0080\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0016\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0057\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0084\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must retrieve facts unavailable from the user's request across the profile, two orders, and two products, while resolving what 'more fancy' means sufficiently to select a theme.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0005\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0194\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0183\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0188\"}]}},\"overall_score\":75,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"Request the fallback boot exchange and the puzzle exchange in their respective delivered orders, after explicit confirmation; an exchange request triggers return instructions by email rather than a new order.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0084\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0082\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"A sufficient path authenticates by name and ZIP, locates and checks both orders, retrieves their product variants and payment method, resolves the puzzle theme, and obtains explicit confirmation before each exchange. The decisive branch is the policy's different-option requirement: it rules out identical-spec boots and selects the user's size-9 leather waterproof fallback. No identical-spec exchange attempt, return, new order, or human transfer is necessary on this path.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Substantial two-order work with conditional preference handling, multi-record tool binding, confirmations, and a qualitative theme clarification yields levels 3/3/3/3/3; 5 × 15 = 75.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"'More fancy' does not uniquely specify fantasy; clarification may be needed before choosing the referenced variant.\",\"The scenario does not explicitly supply the order IDs or payment-method ID to the agent; the initial records are design context rather than agent knowledge.\",\"The policy prohibits same-option exchange, but the precise wording used to explain that restriction to the user is not specified.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Reference actions describe intended work, not observed execution or authoritative ordering.\",\"No workflow or milestone list is supplied; the assessment uses the scenario, completion requirements, policy, tool contracts, and initial design records.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
